+    ~chatplayer("The Burgher is both wise and perceptive.");
+    ~fris_mawnis("Ha! Fortunately for you he also has a sense of humour.");
+    return;
+}
+~fris_mawnis("Hmmmm. Guard! Who is this outlander who has been brought before me?");
+~fris_fridleif("Sire, this is the one who has been honoured with a Fremennik name. A rare honour indeed, for an outlander.");
+~fris_mawnis("You jest! <~fris_he> doesn't look that impressive to me.");
+~chatplayer("Ahem. I am indeed known as <~fris_name> by those in Rellekka. If I am the one you seek, then how may I assist you?");
+~fris_mawnis("Well, I have sought an audience with you for several days now. I have need for a courageous and valiant individual. One who will not flee at the sight of a few trolls.");
+~chatplayer("Ha! It is trolls that fear me! I am Fremennik!");
+~fris_mawnis("Ha! Well said! However, this is no jesting matter. Although a Fremennik name goes a great way towards gaining my trust, I must ask that you prove your loyalty to me and my kinsfolk.");
+~fris_fridleif("Sire, surely that isn't necessary! Anyone who has done the Fremennik Trials can be trusted.");
+~fris_mawnis("Trust me Fridleif, I think in this case it is necessary. Anyway, there are many tasks that need to be done. Some of them are menial, and <~fris_name> needs to show me that <~fris_he> can handle these as well as the ones that simply require bravery. We on Neitiznot are warriors, but we are not just warriors.");
+~fris_fridleif("I apologise for speaking out of turn. The Burgher is wise as always.");
+~chatplayer("I would be honoured to assist you and your tribe, Burgher Burowgar. Indeed I expected no less. This sort of thing seems to happen to me a lot.");
+~fris_mawnis("Good. Thakkrad, which tasks remain?");
+~fris_thakkrad("There are a few building projects that could do with a strong extra hand.");
+~fris_mawnis("Well then, <~fris_name>, are you willing to assist my engineer?");
+~chatplayer("Of course, Mawnis Burowgar.");
+~fris_thakkrad("The bridges to the troll islands need repairing if we are to send a party over. First of all, we will need eight lengths of rope; maybe <~fris_name> could assist me with this.");
+%varb3311_fris_quest = ^fris_need_rope;
+if (inv_total(inv, rope) >= 8) {
+    ~chatplayer("As it happens, I'm carrying enough rope on me right now.");
+    ~fris_rope_show;
+    return;
+}
+if (inv_total(inv, cert_rope) >= 8) {
+    ~chatplayer("As it happens, I'm carrying a note for enough rope on me right now.");
+    ~fris_mawnis("A note? How do you fix a bridge with a note? Go bring me some real rope.");
+    return;
+}
+if (inv_total(bank, rope) >= 8) {
+    ~chatplayer("Right! I'll just go to the bank and get some rope.");
+    ~fris_mawnis("Bank? Why do you need to go to a bank? Neitiznot is the home of quality rope. The hairs of the local yak have the perfect combination of strength and hardiness required from modern rope. Yak rope is stronger and better than any other rope.");
+    ~chatplayer("I thought rope was made from wool. Not yak hair.");
+    ~fris_mawnis("Wool? Wool? What a load of old rope. Wool would make awful rope - it's far too soft and it would soak up the water too easily.");
+    ~chatplayer("So how come Ned from Draynor makes rope out of wool?");
+    ~fris_mawnis("Ned? I don't know anything about Ned. I do know we make regular trades with someone in that area. We send them rope, and we get wool in return.");
+    ~chatplayer("So Ned doesn't make the rope? What a fraud! He had me fooled for so long. Anyway, so that means that all rope is made by Neitiznot from yak hair. So if I happen to have some rope in the bank then that would also be made from high quality Neitiznot yak hair, and I could just give you the rope I already have, rather than make more rope?");
+    ~fris_mawnis("I suppose so. You should really try to make some rope yourself though. Fighting the dual challenges of the yak's hooves and its smell is part of becoming a man over here.");
+    ~chatplayer("I've had enough of strange 'coming of age' rituals for the time being. I'm going to go to the bank and get the rope you need.");
+    ~fris_mawnis("Suit yourself.");
